#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Traditional Finance 🏦]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[
- Assumes investor rationality 🧠
- Assumes market efficiency 📈
]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Traditional finance assumes that investors are rational and markets are efficient.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Behavioral Finance 🧐]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[
- Studies impact of psychological factors 🧠💭
- Suggests investors are influenced by biases 🎭
- Argues markets can be inefficient 📉
]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("In contrast, behavioral finance studies how psychological factors affect financial decisions and market outcomes. It suggests that investors are influenced by biases and that markets can be inefficient as a result.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Key Differences 🔑]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[
- Rationality assumption 🧠 vs. Psychological biases 🎭
- Market efficiency 📈 vs. Market inefficiencies 📉
- Passive strategies 🤖 vs. Active strategies 🏃‍♂️
]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("The key differences between traditional and behavioral finance lie in their assumptions about investor rationality, market efficiency, and the resulting investment strategies. Traditional finance assumes rationality and efficiency, leading to passive strategies, while behavioral finance highlights psychological biases and inefficiencies, suggesting active strategies.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Recap 🎬]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[
- Traditional finance: rationality & efficiency 🧠📈
- Behavioral finance: psychological biases & inefficiencies 🎭📉
- Different assumptions lead to different strategies 🤖🏃‍♂️
]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("To recap, traditional finance assumes investor rationality and market efficiency, while behavioral finance emphasizes the impact of psychological biases on investor behavior and argues that markets can be inefficient. These different assumptions lead to different investment strategies, with traditional finance favoring passive approaches and behavioral finance suggesting active strategies to exploit market inefficiencies.")
]
]